The formula P is a state-level formula, but it was used as a PROPERTY (or PROPERTIES), where a temporal formula is typically expected. State-level formulas used as PROPERTY or PROPERTIES are only checked in the initial state. To verify that the formula P holds in all states of every behavior, use INVARIANT P instead. Alternatively, applying the "always" temporal operator ([]) to the state-level formula P changes it into a temporal formula, asserting that P holds in all states of every behavior. See https://explain.tlapl.us/invariants-and-properties for additional details.
